; claude: a paint program's engine, from scratch, for teaching what
; MacPaint (Bill Atkinson, 1984) actually did (see
; docs/claude_notes/plans/plan_gui_teaching.md, phase 11): a picture as
; a grid of bits (Bitmap), the 8x8 patterns it is painted with
; (Pattern), the lines, brushes and ovals painted into it (Paint), the
; bucket (Seed_fill); the way a picture was written to a floppy,
; PackBits, is libs/compression's (the Amiga's ILBM pictures use it too).
;
; Independent of everything but compression -- no gui, no playground: a
; picture is bits. A private library, installed as part of elm_playground: pure
; OCaml, so every backend can use it (graphics/2d is the software
; backend's, and cannot be).
(library
 (name appkit_paint)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries compression) ; Packbits
)
